{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"UNBLOCKED. Workaround for bug seaworthy-revengeful-blobfish (stale-head): `rebar transition <id> open in_progress --ref HEAD` succeeds where `claim` (no --ref option) does not, because --ref HEAD pins the review/sign step to the reviewing worktree's own HEAD instead of the buggy default fail-safe currency check. Sequence that worked: (1) review-plan --ref HEAD on the epic surfaced ONE real content finding (epic AC1 overstated material_fingerprint as proving byte-exact reconstruction, inconsistent with celestine's already-corrected normalized-basis language) - fixed via edit_ticket, trimmed under the 8000-char plan-review admission cap; (2) re-ran review-plan --ref HEAD -> PASS, 0 blocking, signed cleanly against worktree HEAD 9a94ef9737fb; (3) `rebar transition 759e-7dc1-675c-4877 open in_progress --ref HEAD` succeeded (first attempt hit a transient 'store 4 commits behind' race, resolved on immediate retry); (4) set assignee to ticket.default_assignee (joeoakhart@navapbc.com) since transition doesn't set it like claim does; (5) claimed celestine-treasonous-ewe via mcp__rebar__claim_ticket (parent no longer open, so no cascade needed) -> in_progress. Commented the workaround onto seaworthy-revengeful-blobfish for future reference; bug's root cause is still unfixed for anyone who doesn't pass --ref HEAD explicitly. Now proceeding to Phase 4: TDD held-out loop on celestine-treasonous-ewe (corpus builder, src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788046741703510771,"uuid":"098ae332-2906-4d59-ad3c-c759f115e8c1"}